The first paragraph introduces the focus on g3error minimization/maximization problems and explains the difference between Integer Linear Programs (ILP) and Mixed Integer Linear Programming (MILP). It also describes how input data is structured into a joint distribution frequency matrix, with additional constraints to satisfy marginal information.

